# Rule order matters: Netlify takes the first match, top to bottom.
#
# 1. the apex redirect, forced, so it beats the real files on the netlify.app host
# 2. internal files, forced, so they lose to nothing
# 3. ads.txt, forced 301 to Journey by Mediavine's hosted file
# 4. retired URLs, 301
# 5. the seven SPA routes: six rewritten to the shell, /articles to its own
#    emitted document
#
# There is deliberately no /* catch-all. Anything that matches no rule and no
# file on disk now falls through to 404.html with a real 404 status, which is
# what Netlify does automatically for a 404.html at the site root. Articles are
# NOT listed here: articles/<slug>.html is a real file, and Netlify serves an
# HTML file for its extensionless path by default, so /articles/<slug> resolves
# without a rule. scripts/pre-render.js asserts both halves of that.

https://dapper-axolotl-1f65df.netlify.app/* https://cyrilica.com/:splat 301!

/scripts/*                      /404.html  404!
/netlify/*                      /404.html  404!
/CLAUDE.md                      /404.html  404!
/README.md                      /404.html  404!
/SECURITY.md                    /404.html  404!

# ads.txt is Journey by Mediavine's hosted file, which Journey keeps current, so
# the site serves no copy of its own. Written in lowercase. scripts/pre-render.js
# asserts this is the only ads.txt rule, that its target is ADS_TXT_URL, that no
# earlier rule matches /ads.txt, and that no ads.txt sits at the root.
/ads.txt https://adstxt.journeymv.com/sites/0f4d724d-efc6-493d-9d37-0ec09bb2dbc1/ads.txt 301!

/articles/cyrillic-alphabet-chart /articles/russian-alphabet-chart 301
/articles/cyrillic-handwriting /articles/practice-writing-cyrillic 301
/articles/common-cyrillic-mistakes /articles/common-mistakes 301
/articles/cyrillic-vs-latin /articles/false-friends 301
/reference /articles/russian-alphabet-chart 301
/articles/the-cyrillic-backwards-r-myth-why-hollywood-gets-it-wrong /articles/backwards-r-myth 301
/articles/cyrillic-pop-culture /articles/backwards-r-myth 301!
/home /  301
/index.html /  301!
# Standalone pages are real files at the site root, so Netlify serves both
# /<slug> and /<slug>.html at 200. Forced, because without the ! the real
# file wins and the duplicate stays reachable. scripts/pre-render.js asserts
# this rule exists for every standalone page, that none is ever rewritten to
# the shell, and that no rule serves /<slug>/ with a 200.
/teachers.html /teachers  301!
/es.html /es  301!
# The /articles listing is emitted to articles.html at the root as well, so
# its own path would be a duplicate at 200. A forced 301 on a rewrite target
# does not affect the rewrite: / and /index.html below already pair the two
# the same way. scripts/pre-render.js asserts this rule and the rewrite.
/articles.html /articles  301!

# The seven SPA routes. Generated from VALID_PAGES in js/core.js and asserted
# against it at build time, so this list cannot drift from the router. Six are
# rewritten to the shell. /articles is rewritten to articles.html, the listing
# emitted by scripts/pre-render.js as its own document; on the shell the router
# still shows the listing in-app.
/            /index.html  200
/articles    /articles.html  200
/settings    /index.html  200
/about       /index.html  200
/contact     /index.html  200
/privacy     /index.html  200
/terms       /index.html  200
